extends RefCounted

## Shared Medieval rules plus only the selected difficulty's mechanics.
const COMMON: String = "CONTROLS\n• Spectator mode beside difficulty launches four AI armies with no player; use camera controls to watch. The fast-forward icon cycles 1x → 2x → 4x → 8x → 1x in any Medieval match; every new match starts at 1x.\n• L-click or drag a box to select; click a tile to move or an enemy to focus.\n• R-click drag / Space-drag: pan · Wheel: zoom · A: select all · Esc: pause\n\nCAPTURE & HEAL\n• Only seated warriors capture spades/hearts/eligible bases; more allies capture faster. Any living opponent in the tile pauses all capture progress, including moving or fighting opponents. Progress resumes when uncontested; friendly units do not block each other.\n• Human capture times: 1/2/3/4/5/6+ seated warriors take 12/9/6/4/2/1 seconds. Other races: 16.7 seconds divided by seated warriors.\n• Partial capture progress stays when you leave. Original bases require their original race to be eliminated. Conquered bases can be recaptured while their current owner lives.\n• Each captured enemy base adds 6 capacity; losing it removes that bonus. Spawn speed stays unchanged. Spawns alternate across owned bases in order.\n• Owned spades speed spawning; for demons, owned hearts provide the same spawning boost. Owned hearts and bases heal seated warriors at 1.8 HP/sec; demons heal only at bases, never hearts.\n• Elves heal at 3.6 HP/sec on owned hearts; base healing is unchanged. Elves must be sitting and unattacked for 3 seconds to heal.\n\nSPAWNING & COMBAT\n• Orcs spawn twice as fast. All races start with 12 capacity.\n• Orcs gain +1 capacity per two owned spades or hearts. Converted orcs are shown as (+N) and do not consume spawn capacity.\n• Melee warriors surround enemies; upgraded humans and elves can attack from farther away.\n• Ranged attacks (reach above 1 cell): 80% hit chance against stationary targets. Moving targets: compare attacker swings/sec to target movement multiplier; faster/equal/slower gives 70%/50%/30%. Melee: 90% against stationary targets; cannot hit moving targets.\n• Each additional orc engaged on the same target deals +1 punch damage.\n• Humans: kills repeat +2 max HP, +2 punch, then +2 attack reach, scaling without a tier cap. Humans hit one target per swing. Fighting on owned tiles grants +1 punch, lasting 3 seconds after leaving.\n• Orc killing blows: 25/50/75/100% conversion chance for 1/2/3/4+ distinct orcs that hit the victim in the last 3 seconds, even above capacity. Converted orcs inherit maximum HP up to 30 and permanent punch up to 10 and spawn at that capped full HP; they use orc group damage, with final punch still capped at 10; reach resets to 1 cell. Temporary bonuses are not inherited.\n• Elves: +1 max HP per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds. Every 3 bonus HP adds 1 cell reach, scaling without a tier cap.\n• Demons: +1 punch per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds. Demon killers heal 3 HP; assisting demons heal 1 HP when their last hit was within 3 seconds. Healing is capped at max HP; killers do not also receive assist healing. Enemy demons never retreat to heal. At 8/12/18 punch, movement speed is +20%/+30%/+40%.\n• Assist credit is once per death; HP bonuses do not instantly heal. Bonuses reset on respawn. Eliminate all opponents to win.\n• Assigned units clear enemies on their ordered tile together without chasing outside it. Increased-range units can stop before entering and fire at enemies on that tile as soon as they are in reach. Once clear, stand for 1 second, then sit to capture. After capture, hold and defend until a new command.\n• Melee guards on owned tiles react to enemies within 1 movement cell of the border and may pursue into one directly adjacent tile before returning. Increased-range guards instead detect and fire at enemies within their own attack range while staying on their defending tile. Idle defenders retaliate when hit if their orders permit. Enemy ranged-fire responses apply on every difficulty: human tile defenders share a 50/50 pursue-to-death or retreat choice; elf defenders share a 50/50 pursuit or relocation choice, retaining low-HP recovery. Orcs decide individually: pursue, but flee if outnumbered by attackers within 2 tiles or at 20% HP or less, subject to their 30-second cooldown and 10-second flee window. Demons pursue as a group, then roll once to flee (50%) or keep fighting after losing at least half the original group. Counter-pursuit has no tile leash; strategic orders do not interrupt these commitments. Explicit player and enemy-planner orders can assign new destinations.\n• Enemy AI units in an invaded owned base attack intruders after their short spawn-standing animation, even during the opening delay. Clear invaders inside the base before engaging border threats or taking other orders.\n• Enemy retreat labels stay overhead while active: humans \"Retreat!\", orcs \"Flee!\", elves \"Fallback!\". Fleeing enemy orcs gain 30% movement speed throughout both halves of their flee window. If no capture tile exists in the chosen quadrant, they hold a safe position there instead.\n• Difficulty does not change spawn rates; racial, spade and demon-heart bonuses still apply.\n"
const RULES: Array[String] = [
	"EASY AI\n• Enemy units act individually after the opening idle delay (about 22 seconds), choosing capture, attack or healing orders.\n• No strategic squads. Shared ranged-fire response groups and orc flee cooldowns still apply. Wounded units other than demons can seek owned hearts/bases through the individual AI.\n",
	"NORMAL AI\n• Enemy squads coordinate after an opening delay of about 22 seconds. Decisions occur every 2 seconds, with local enemy awareness (16 movement cells).\n• Groups usually contain 2–4 units; five recruits split into groups of 3 and 2. Groups share capture and attack orders.\n• Humans capture and fight together. Orcs focus one enemy; when locally outnumbered, they flee for 10 seconds, once every 30 seconds: first 5 seconds toward the quadrant with the fewest enemies, then 5 seconds seeking a capture tile there, prioritising uncontested tiles.\n• Elves retreat below 20% HP toward an owned heart/base and recover to 80%. If threatened, they randomly fight back or relocate. No ten-cell healing limit or timed healing cooldown applies.\n• Demons favour weak nearby victims and compare their group's strength with nearby defenders before attacking.\n",
	"EXPERT AI & BONUSES\n• Enemy AI starts immediately. If no capturable objectives or local enemies remain, groups advance to find surviving opponents rather than waiting indefinitely. Decisions occur every second, with local enemy awareness (16 movement cells).\n• Enemy humans fill groups to 4 and choose capture targets within five capture tiles, preferring no enemies. They commit and fight for the chosen tile. If none is visible, they scout locally to discover more tiles instead of waiting at base. Losing half the original mission group gives one 50% retreat chance; a retreat goes to the nearest owned heart/base without a range limit, has a 45-second cooldown and lasts until full HP. \n• Orcs fill groups to 6 and focus one enemy. Locally outnumbered orcs flee for 10 seconds, once every 30 seconds: first 5 seconds toward the least-enemy quadrant, then 5 seconds seeking a capture tile there, prioritising uncontested tiles.\n• Enemy elves gain +2 maximum HP per kill or damaging assist (player elves remain +1). All Expert demons gain +2 punch per kill and +1 punch per damaging assist within 3 seconds. Movement speed increases by 5% per complete 2 bonus punch: 7/9/11 total punch gives +5%/+10%/+15%, continuing without the old tier cap.\n• Elves form groups of up to 4 core units; elves with unlocked range may join full groups. Groups prefer separated destinations.\n• Elf priority: heal → protect wounded allies within 10 movement cells → capture → group attacks.\n• At 20% HP or less, elves may retreat only to an owned heart/base within 10 movement cells. Healing-retreat cooldown: 45 seconds from retreat start. They stay until 100% HP.\n• Demons form groups of up to 4. Priority: defend owned tiles within 10 movement cells → capture → group attacks. They never retreat to heal.\n• Healing cooldowns prevent starting another retreat, not an ongoing recovery. No nearby healing point means no retreat and no cooldown spent. Distance is Manhattan distance to the nearest cell on the healing tile.\n"
]
const TOOLTIPS: Array[String] = [
	"Easy: individual enemy decisions with an opening delay of about 22 seconds. Clear the ordered tile, stand for 1 second, then capture and defend within one adjacent tile.",
	"Normal: coordinated groups of 2–4, opening delay of about 22 seconds, local awareness, race-specific combat and retreats. Ordered-tile defence is limited to one adjacent tile.",
	"Expert: no opening delay, race-specific group sizes and priorities, nearby healing with cooldowns. Local awareness and standard spawn rates. Ordered-tile defence is limited to one adjacent tile."
]


static func text(difficulty: int) -> String:
	var selected: int = clampi(difficulty, 0, RULES.size() - 1)
	var shared: String = COMMON
	if selected == ClassicSimulation.Difficulty.EXPERT:
		shared = shared.replace("Elves: +1 max HP per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds.", "Elves: player units gain +1 max HP and enemy AI units gain +2 max HP per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds.")
		shared = shared.replace("Demons: +1 punch per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds.", "Demons: +2 punch per kill and +1 punch per damaging assist within 3 seconds, for both player and enemy units.")
		shared = shared.replace("At 8/12/18 punch, movement speed is +20%/+30%/+40%.", "Every complete 2 bonus punch adds 5% movement speed (7/9/11 total punch gives +5%/+10%/+15%, and so on).")
	return RULES[selected] + "\n" + shared


static func tooltip(difficulty: int) -> String:
	return TOOLTIPS[clampi(difficulty, 0, TOOLTIPS.size() - 1)]
